From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 02:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2712/2713] arm64: dts: qcom: mahua-hp-omnibook-5-bf1xxx: Build
 on Linux 7.3

The tree is written against qcom-next, whose glymur.dtsi adds the APSS
CoreSight trace path, and it disables those nodes by path. Linux 7.3
has none of them, so dtc stops at the first missing path. Drop the
overrides.

The tree also turns on the Adreno X2-85 GPU, which Linux 7.3 doesn't
support yet. msm binds the GPU into the same DRM device as the display,
so a GPU that never probes keeps the panel down too. Leave the GPU
block off, as the .dtsi has it and as the ThinkPad T14s Gen 7's and the
OmniBook X16's trees do, until the kernel supports the X2-85.

Build the tree.

Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
